Canned_Dinosaur said:
I’m sure you understand that there was no way for me to tell what stage you were at without seeing how you’ve implemented things. So please share how exactly you’ve implemented the costs. Also, please consider reviewing the
support template
to refresh your memory as to what is typically needed for effective support!
Click to expand...
I am in no way downplaying the support you are giving me. I am even very thankful for taking the time to try to help me.
Here's a skill i've done for better context:
For JS: Draw Gauge, I don't know what to do. I don't know how to code nor what to tweak to get The result I want.
I saw this in the Plugin:
*
@param
GaugeDrawJS:func
* @text JS: Draw Gauge
* @parent  Gauges
* @type note
*
@desc
Code to determine how to draw the Skill Cost resource for this gauge type.
*
@Default
"// Declare Variables
const sprite = this;
const settings = sprite._costSettings;
const bitmap = sprite.bitmap;
const user = sprite._battler;
const currentValue = sprite.currentDisplayedValue();

// Draw Gauge
const color1 = ColorManager.textColor(30);
const color2 = ColorManager.textColor(31);
const gx = 0;
const gy = sprite.bitmapHeight() - sprite.gaugeHeight();
const gw = sprite.bitmapWidth() - gx;
const gh = sprite.gaugeHeight();
this.drawFullGauge(color1, color2, gx, gy, gw, gh);

// Draw Label
const label = settings.Name;
const lx = 4;
const ly = 0;
const lw = sprite.bitmapWidth();
const lh = sprite.bitmapHeight();
sprite.setupLabelFont();
bitmap.paintOpacity = 255;
bitmap.drawText(label, lx, ly, lw, lh, "left");

// Draw Value
const vw = sprite.bitmapWidth() - 2;
const vh = sprite.bitmapHeight();
sprite.setupValueFont();
bitmap.textColor = ColorManager.normalColor();
bitmap.drawText(currentValue, 0, 0, vw, vh, "right");"
But to be honest I don't understand a single Thing.

There's already a line of code in the VS Skill Cost Types how they draw an icon in there, like in the 'Potion' one at least. Just copy that and add more icons (increase the x spot (the first 0) by 24 each time) LOL. And remove the stuff where it draws the gauge. Then just make conditionals there that if a property/variable (ammo in chamber) is 5, all the icons are the index for white icon, otherwise start adding black ones at the last spots.
EDIT: I mean like in JS Draw Gauge
bitmap.blt(iconBitmap, sx, sy, pw, ph, 0, 0, 24, 24);

I assume since you're doing it with items that you have only 1 character using that class.
Here's an example for the JS draw gauge. Max bullets is currently at 5 and there's no label text, because the default area is so small that if you try to add more than 5 icons or add the text, it cuts off. You can check for yourself if you want to increase the area, I'll leave below the codes to add the "Ammo" label and make it reference maxItems.
(There might be some unnecessary lines left, because I didn't have the energy to check everything, but the extra line shouldn't matter.)
// Declare Settings
// Declare Variables
const sprite = this;
const settings = sprite._costSettings;
const bitmap = sprite.bitmap;
const user = sprite._battler;
const item = $dataItems[7];
const currentValue = sprite.currentDisplayedValue();
const bitmapWidth = sprite.bitmapWidth();
const bitmapHeight = sprite.textHeight ? sprite.textHeight() : sprite.bitmapHeight();
const gaugeHeight = sprite.gaugeHeight();
// Draw Gauge
// Draw Value
// Draw Icon
const bullets = $gameParty.numItems(item)
const maxBullets = 5
const emptyChambers = maxBullets - bullets;
const iconIndex = 10;
const iconIndexEmpty = 26;
const iconBitmap = ImageManager.loadSystem("IconSet");
const pw = ImageManager.iconWidth;
const ph = ImageManager.iconHeight;
const sx = (iconIndex % 16) * pw;
const sx2 = (iconIndexEmpty % 16) * pw;
const sy = Math.floor(iconIndex / 16) * ph;
const sy2 = Math.floor(iconIndexEmpty / 16) * ph;
let emptyStart = 0;
for (let i=1; i<=bullets; i++) {
bitmap.blt(iconBitmap, sx, sy, pw, ph, (i-1)*24, 0, 24, 24);
emptyStart += 1;
}
for (let i=1; i<=emptyChambers; i++) {
bitmap.blt(iconBitmap, sx2, sy2, pw, ph, (emptyStart+i-1)*24, 0, 24, 24);
}
///////////////////////////////////
ADD LABEL:
// Draw Label
const label = "Ammo";
const lx = 0;
const ly = 0;
const lw = sprite.bitmapWidth();
const lh = sprite.bitmapHeight();
sprite.setupLabelFont();
bitmap.paintOpacity = 255;
bitmap.drawText(label, lx, ly, lw, lh, "left");
REFERENCE MAX ITEMS (change line above to):
const maxBullets = $gameParty.maxItems(item);
